@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:maintenance] vendored-source-boundary
Vendored assets MUST retain their license/provenance notices. Application
behavior and contract backfills belong in the integrating hooks or directory
contracts, not edits to bundled upstream code. A demonstrated upstream defect MAY
receive a narrowly scoped local correction only with recorded original and patched
integrity, reproducible patch instructions, an architecture review and a regression
executing the patched artifact. An intentional vendor update MUST review affected
hooks and rebuild the application's asset bundles.
